  "system": {
    "identifier": "fire-release-wildfire",
    "description": "<p>You manifest a multicolored flame and Fire a stream of it towards a creature you can see within range. Target creature must make a Dexterity saving throw. On a failed save they gain 2 ranks of the Burned condition, and take 1d12+1 Fire damage. On a successful save they gain 1 rank of burned and no further effects.</p>\n<p>If the target already had the Burned condition, on a failed save, you trigger the Burned conditions damage effect as if it were the start of that creature turn.</p>",
